{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299610-pc-vs-the-consensus","id":1299610,"title":"PC vs the consensus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-25T08:54:23-07:00","id":1299610,"title":"PC vs the consensus","content":"So I had an idea to have a player who is being driven to find a way to change the consensus and thus alter reality. <br /> <br /> He\u2019s a reincarnation of Diogenes. Which btw if you read the real story is pretty juicy plot material. <br /> <br /> Have any of you touched this plot thread before? How did it go? Is it too abstract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:27:34-07:00","id":1299662,"title":"","content":"Can't say I have, but it sure sounds like Mage.<br /> <br /> In M20 there's <i>Crazy Wisdom</i> Practice which it's very &quot;Diogenes&quot;, as it's all about challenging society's preconceptions.<br /> <br /> All mages tend to do a thing or two to change the consensus, however, as a main goal changing the consensus it's a very &quot;social manipulation&quot; thing to do. It signifies that you care about what other people thinks (and want to change it). In Mage this has been mostly achieved by shadowy illuminaty conspiracies. It's the speciality of the Technocracy in general and the NWO in particular for a reason.<br /> <br /> In my opinion a cynic would rather <i>reject </i>the whole idea of the consensus than try to <i>change </i>it. Doing what he believes to be better and not caring much about what people wants to believe. Teaching mostly with the example, and if people refuses to follow suit, worse for them.<br /> <br /> If you think about it, the power over the consensus sits over a giant lie: That what people believes<i> its</i> <i>actually true</i>, rather than just a temporary agreement. I imagine that, for someone interested in moral virtue over any other sort of excelency, the factions that fight over that giant lie would seem quite evil (they speak about order and freedom, but the conclusion it's just more power for them).<br /> <br /> If these musings are too abstract or not depends on your ability to bring it to ground. I think a character motivated by molesting the preconceptions of others can be fun...but also a pain in the arse (like Diogenes surely was). It seems very easy to be &quot;that guy&quot; always trolling the party if you don't moderate it. It could be useful to remember that he has a very Diogenes vive, but he's not Diogenes. He probably needs some specific short term goals to explain why he's in the cabal rather than sleeping in an alley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T00:05:46-07:00","id":1299874,"title":"","content":"Diogenes challenges truth. So I think his overarching goal would be to remove lies. Doing that would disarm many people with guile. All sides would not want that. So enemies would abound if they knew. <br /> <br /> Basically. If I were successful subterfuge would go away. All manner of supernatural would be exposed and society would flip on its axel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T06:20:00-07:00","id":1299936,"title":"","content":"The character you're describing sounds like he matches up very well with the Taftani philosophy.<br /> <br /> Show people &quot;The Truth&quot; (meaning magic) by doing magic right in front of them until you eventually force them to acknowledge that it's real. Be prepared to go out in a spectacular conflagration of Paradox, because no one ever said doing the right thing was easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","name":"gx240","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}